==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Seal]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*5 [[Pigge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[MikuBear]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Snow Miku 2021 (Enemy)|Snow Miku 2021]] spawns as the boss.
**4 [[MikuBear]]s spawn, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
**3 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 30~33.33 seconds<sup>900f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Gory]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage is incredibly annoying even on 1-crown. As if the buffed Angelic Gories aren't bad enough, Gabriels can easily maintain ground and block hits for other enemies. Snow Miku's 600-range Omni Strike will beat any backliners into submission while MikuBear finish any survivors.

Since three Angelic Gories spawn on a timer, it's recommended to lure and remove them before hitting the base, or else their overwhelming combined DPS will simply demolish everything. As soon as they're gone, send units to finish off Snow Miku and destroy the base for the Timed Score Rewards.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone]] - Stone's massive health means it won't fall during its brief lifetime and has the speed to maintain a defensive line with Research Combos. It is a welcome addition anywhere, but is practically mandatory on 2-3 crown to hold them back.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] - With the Extra Money and Move Speed Up Talents, Can Can eases the startoff significantly, able to pick off Angelic Gories and Gabriels with sufficient support, and also comes in handy for cleanup.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - This frail melee rusher's extreme DPS and very high speed can be put to good use at any point in the stage with precise timing and significant support. He can juggle groups of Angelic Gories as he keeps his distance from Snow Miku's Omni Strike. Once the threats are clear, he can be deployed to steamroll what's left of this stage.

